.TH SIGROK\-FWEXTRACT\-INTRONIX\-LOGICPORT 1 "October 18, 2026"
.SH "NAME"
sigrok\-fwextract\-intronix\-logicport \- Extract Intronix LogicPort bitstreams
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B sigrok\-fwextract\-intronix\-logicport [\-o DIR] FILE
.br
.B sigrok\-fwextract\-intronix\-logicport [\-o DIR] \-d
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
This tool extracts the FPGA bitstreams for the Intronix LogicPort LA1034
USB logic analyzer from the vendor software. The FPGA is volatile and gets
configured by the libsigrok driver with one of eight bitstreams, depending
on the sampling mode (timing SDR, timing DDR at 500MHz, and several state
mode variants).
.PP
The bitstreams ship in a file called "LogicPort.ccf", inside the vendor's
Windows installer [1]. The tool takes either LogicPort.ccf (from an
installed copy of the software) or the installer itself, or it can
download the installer. Unpacking the installer needs 7\-Zip (7zz, 7z or
7za), as the file is Deflate64 compressed. To download and extract the
bitstreams, run:
.PP
.B "  $ sigrok-fwextract-intronix-logicport -d"
.br
.RB "  Downloading https://www.pctestinstruments.com/downloads/logicport_2371.exe"
.br
.RB "  saved 66115 bytes to intronix-logicport-state-after.rbf (crc32 fb28768e)"
.br
.RB "  saved 65282 bytes to intronix-logicport-state-before-clk1-rise.rbf (crc32 a079b32c)"
.br
.RB "  saved 65431 bytes to intronix-logicport-state-before-clk2-rise.rbf (crc32 5664f7d7)"
.br
.RB "  saved 65458 bytes to intronix-logicport-state-before-clk1-fall.rbf (crc32 e344d08b)"
.br
.RB "  saved 65407 bytes to intronix-logicport-state-before-clk2-fall.rbf (crc32 bdc060a8)"
.br
.RB "  saved 65937 bytes to intronix-logicport-state-on.rbf (crc32 832c3e3f)"
.br
.RB "  saved 64452 bytes to intronix-logicport-timing-ddr.rbf (crc32 ece870e6)"
.br
.RB "  saved 66149 bytes to intronix-logicport-timing-sdr.rbf (crc32 70a7a41d)"
.PP
The output above is for LogicPort software build 2371. Copy the resulting
files to the location where libsigrok expects to find firmware files.
By default this is /usr/local/share/sigrok\-firmware.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-download
Download the vendor installer [1] instead of reading FILE.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output\-dir DIR
Write the files to DIR instead of the current directory.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Exits with 0 on success, 1 on most failures.
